rue},{"title":"Budget Management 2025-26, Q2","url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22202/budget-management-2025-26-q2.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"17/11/2025","key":true},{"title":"Q1 Budget Management 2025-26","url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s21853/q1-budget-management-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"15/09/2025","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-16","committee":"Cabinet","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-24","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-09","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-07","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Scrutiny Committee People and Communities","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Cabinet","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Scrutiny Committee Place and Environment","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Freedom of Information request volumes up 20% year-on-year; statutory compliance target missed.","lead":"Compliance failure is an audit finding. Rising FOI volumes suggest increased external scrutiny and under-resourced legal teams create risks of further compliance breaches.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Budget Management 2026/27 - Q1.","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s24003/24003.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Resource gaps across legal, finance, HR and planning funded from reserves rather than sustainable budget.","lead":"Staffing gaps in finance and legal functions directly affect governance and financial control. Funding core staffing pressures from reserves rather than sustainable budget carries risk. Market-driven recruitment failure suggests sector-wide constraints.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Budget Management 2026/27 - Q1.","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s24003/24003.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Significant budget deficit emerging from 2027/28 following the Final Local Government Settlement.","lead":"A lender needs to understand whether a council can sustain service delivery from its own revenues. A multi-year structural deficit is material to creditworthiness and the council's ability to service debt.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Budget Management 2026/27 - Q1.","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s24003/24003.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Management 2026/27 - Q1.","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s24003/24003.pdf","headline":"Freedom of Information request volumes up 20% year-on-year; statutory compliance target missed.","detail":"FOI requests rose from 172 in Q1 2025/26 to 214 in Q1 2026/27. Compliance with the statutory 20-working-day response requirement fell to 94%, missing the 100% target. The council attributes this to volume growth straining legal resources. Performance did improve from 80.9% at year-end 2025/26, but the upward trend continues.","category":"governance","matters":"Compliance failure is an audit finding. Rising FOI volumes suggest increased external scrutiny and under-resourced legal teams create risks of further compliance breaches.","figures":"FOI requests: 214 (Q1 26/27) vs 172 (Q1 25/26), 20% increase; compliance 94% vs 100% target; year-end 25/26 compliance was 80.9%","quote":"The percentage of Freedom of Information Requests responded to within 20 working days fell short of the 100% target at 94%. This is due to a year on year increase in volumes of requests received, up from 172 in Q1 2025/26 to 214 this period, which is representative of 20% more.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Management 2026/27 - Q1.","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s24003/24003.pdf","headline":"Resource gaps across legal, finance, HR and planning funded from reserves rather than sustainable budget.","detail":"The council reports ongoing additional resource requirements across legal, finance, comms, HR and planning, particularly for speculative development activity. Market constraints are preventing recruitment of specialist expertise. The council is using intern pipeline and contract staff funded from the Project & Efficiency reserve. Q1 treasury receipts of \u00a3215k are being allocated to this reserve for LGR, Joint Venture and Simpler Recycling project delivery.","category":"people","matters":"Staffing gaps in finance and legal functions directly affect governance and financial control. Funding core staffing pressures from reserves rather than sustainable budget carries risk. Market-driven recruitment failure suggests sector-wide constraints.","figures":"\u00a3215k Q1 treasury receipts allocated to Project & Efficiency reserve for additional staffing support; resource requirements identified as ongoing across legal, finance, comms, HR, planning","quote":"There have been and continue to be, additional resource requirements in legal, finance, comms, HR and planning (particularly in response to speculative development activity). Funds being set aside in the Project and Efficiency reserve have been secured to underpin delivery across a range of complex and high-priority projects, including the Joint Venture (JV), Simpler Recycling, and Local Government Reorganisation (LGR), where market constraints have impacted the ability to secure specialist expertise","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Management 2026/27 - Q1.","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s24003/24003.pdf","headline":"Significant budget deficit emerging from 2027/28 following the Final Local Government Settlement.","detail":"The council explicitly identifies a structural deficit from 2027/28 onwards resulting from the Final Local Government Settlement. This is driving the decision to allocate Q1 treasury receipts (\u00a3430k) partly to reserves as 'prudent financial management' to support medium-term financial resilience rather than using them for current spending.","category":"income","matters":"A lender needs to understand whether a council can sustain service delivery from its own revenues. A multi-year structural deficit is material to creditworthiness and the council's ability to service debt.","figures":"Significant deficit from 2027/28 onwards; Q1 treasury receipts \u00a3430k; \u00a3215k allocated to Project & Efficiency reserve, \u00a3215k to General Reserve","quote":"This prudent financial management is even more necessary after the outcome of the Final Local Government Settlement, which created a significant deficit for the Council from 2027/28 onwards.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-07","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Item 1 - Treasury Management Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s23273/23273.pdf","headline":"The council's \u00a36m commercial property fund investment has fallen to \u00a35.470m, a loss of \u00a3530k reflecting UK property market decline.","detail":"Mid Sussex holds \u00a35.470m in the Local Authorities' Property Fund as of 31 March 2026, down from \u00a36m invested. The report explicitly attributes this to the general decline in commercial property prices in the UK. The council has set aside a provision in reserves against the risk of this decline relating to the IFRS9 statutory override, which extends only to March 2029. The fund generated \u00a3255k dividend income in 2025/26.","category":"reserves","matters":"A significant unrealised loss on a pooled investment fund indicates exposure to commercial property market risk. The need to provision against further potential losses directly impacts the council's reserves and balance sheet strength, which lenders consider when assessing creditworthiness and capacity to manage financial shocks.","figures":"\u00a35.470m current value (from \u00a36m invested); \u00a3530k loss; \u00a3255k dividend income in 2025/26","quote":"The Fund was valued at 31 March 2026 at \u00a35.470m. This reflects the general decline in commercial property prices in the UK. A provision has been set aside in reserves for any risk of this decline relating to the IFRS9 statutory override ending","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-06","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Management 2025-26 \u2013 Outturn Report","paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s23390/23390.pdf","headline":"Abandoned vehicles service performance deteriorated from 97% to 62% resolution rate, expected to continue into 2026/27","detail":"The percentage of abandoned vehicles cases resolved within seven days has declined throughout the year from 97% in Q1 to 62% in Q4 due to delay in a system change used county-wide with Sussex Police and the County Council. The service has flagged that this slippage may continue to be a challenge in the first half of 2026/27.","category":"governance","matters":"Significant operational performance deterioration flagged as likely to persist, indicating an unresolved system issue affecting service delivery","figures":"Abandoned vehicles resolution: 97% in Q1, declining to 62% in Q4","quote":"The percentage of abandoned vehicles cases resolved within seven days has been steadily declining throughout the whole year from 97% in Q1 to 62% in Q4 due to a delay in a change of the shared system used county wide with Sussex Police and the County Council. The service area has flagged that this slippage may continue to be a challenge in the first half of 2026/27.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-14"},"name":"Mid Sussex","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-22","since_iso":"2026-08-23","distress":false,"headline":"Freedom of Information request volumes up 20% year-on-year; statutory compliance target missed.","lead":"Compliance failure is an audit finding. Rising FOI volumes suggest increased external scrutiny and under-resourced legal teams create risks of further compliance breaches.","also":["2 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-11-16","n_findings":3,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Budget Management 2026/27 - Q1.","top_paper_url":"https://midsussex.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s24003/24003.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":27,"news_drafts_total":3}}